.TH OPENSVR 1  "opensvr 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
opensvr \- The opensvr command\-line tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBopensvr\fR [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The opensvr command\-line tool
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress progress and non\-error messages
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra detail about what each command is doing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
opensvr\-info(1)
List tracks, voices and whether their files exist
.TP
opensvr\-render(1)
Render a project to a 24\-bit stereo WAV file
.TP
opensvr\-midi(1)
Export notes, lyrics, tempo and meter as a Standard MIDI File
.TP
opensvr\-convert(1)
Convert between project formats (.svp and .mid, matched case\-insensitively)
.TP
opensvr\-complete(1)
Print a shell completion script to stdout
.TP
opensvr\-man(1)
Print a troff man page to stdout (see `opensvr.1`)
.TP
opensvr\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Voice databases and dictionaries are not bundled; point to files you own.
OPENSVR_VOICE and OPENSVR_DICTIONARY default \-\-voice and \-\-dictionary when those flags are absent; explicit flags win.
OPENSVR_MODELS_DIR defaults \-\-models\-dir the same way, resolving Flat voice models away from the document.
\-\-dict and OPENSVR_DICT are accepted as legacy aliases for \-\-dictionary and OPENSVR_DICTIONARY.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 usage error, 2 load error, 3 render/write error, 130 cancelled.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
